In MSTest v4, `[ExpectedException]` was removed. Replace it with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>` (or `Assert.ThrowsExactlyAsync<T>` for async methods) inside the test body:

**Before (v3):**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
public void MyTest()
{
    service.DoSomething(null);
}
```

**After (v4):**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void MyTest()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(
        () => service.DoSomething(null));
}
```

For async:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task MyAsyncTest()
{
    await Assert.ThrowsExactlyAsync<ArgumentNullException>(
        async () => await service.DoSomethingAsync(null));
}
```

This is preferred because it pinpoints exactly which line should throw, avoiding false passes when setup code throws unexpectedly.
